<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mühlhausen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mühlhausen is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unstrut">Unstrut</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, which grew around a royal palace and was an imperial city from the late 12th century until 1802. It was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>. In 1525 the radical preacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-muntzer">Thomas Müntzer</a> made it his base during the Peasants' War, and after his defeat he was executed outside its walls.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhlhausen.jpg" alt="Mühlhausen" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sander · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altstadt_M%C3%BChlhausen.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
